  "bull_bear_summary": {
    "bull_case": "SMCI is the dominant player in AI-optimized server solutions with deep Nvidia GPU partnership. FY2025 revenue of $14.98B (+110% YoY), net income $1.21B. Trading at ~16x FCF while delivering >30% YoY growth. AI-related sales expected to reach $20B over next 4 quarters (surpassing Dell's $15B). Raised FY2026 revenue guidance to $40B+. Liquid-cooled AI systems launch could be a new growth engine. Rack-scale AI strategy (DCBBS) offers faster time-to-deployment than competitors. Stock trading 35% below analyst targets. One analyst sees $60 target by summer 2026.",
    "bear_case": "Gross margins declined for 10 consecutive quarters; Q1 FY2026 gross margin at 9.3% (down from 11.8% in Q4 FY2025). Despite 47% revenue growth in FY2025, operating income declined 1.0% YoY. Net margin fell to 3.4% in Q1 FY2026. Goldman Sachs Sell rating citing structural profitability challenges. Pricing pressure from both suppliers (Nvidia) and hyperscale customers due to intermediary position. Ongoing DOJ investigation into accounting practices. SGA expenses growing rapidly ($1.37B FY2026E vs $754M FY2025E). FMP rating B- with DCF score of just 1/5 and D/E score 1/5."
  },
